{
  "verdict": "LOCAL_ART_IMPROVEMENT",
  "visible_improvements": [
    "The bridge and gate structure now exhibit more consistent material detail and lighting compared to the earlier Unity V4 version. The stone textures are more varied and the shadows cast by the gate and bridge are more defined, improving the sense of depth and realism.",
    "The cliffside geometry has been refined with more naturalistic rock formations and erosion patterns, especially visible in the transition zones around the bridge. The upper bastion remains a greybox, but the surrounding terrain now better integrates with the castle’s silhouette."
  ],
  "remaining_defects": [
    "The upper bastion remains a greybox and lacks architectural detail, which is a persistent issue from the earlier version. The material on the upper walls is still flat and does not convey texture or wear.",
    "The road and stair geometry, while more readable, still appear as simplified, low-poly surfaces. The stair treads lack individual detail and the road surface lacks variation in texture or wear."
  ],
  "protected_regressions": [],
  "next_bounded_edit": "Author a truly separate transition module informed by Qwen and export only that module. Import into Unity in isolated scene and capture paired real before/after. Independently evaluate visual quality and mobile impact; record result here."
}
